7. Why CDN?

                        This is probably the most important component of YouTube's architecture.                        
                        Suppose 1 million people watch the same popular video.
                        
                        Without a CDN:
                                        1 million users
                                               │
                                               ▼
                                        Application Servers
                                               │
                                               ▼
                                        Object Storage

                        That's terrible.  The application layer becomes involved in serving enormous amounts of data.

                Instead:

                                User
                                  │
                                  ▼
                                Nearest CDN Edge
                                  │
                                  ├── Cache HIT ──► Video
                                  │
                                  └── Cache MISS
                                          │
                                          ▼
                                     Origin Storage

================================================================================================================================================================

Why?CDN:
        CDNs provide:
                        
                        geographic proximity
                        caching
                        lower latency
                        massive bandwidth
                        reduced origin load
                        
         So I'd tell the interviewer:
                 “Because video delivery is bandwidth-intensive and geographically distributed, 
                   I'd put a CDN in front of the video origin. Application servers should not stream video bytes.”
                        
         That's a very strong statement.




================================================================================================================================================================
8. Why Object Storage?
                Examples conceptually include:                
                        Google Cloud Storage
                        Amazon S3
                
                We need to store enormous amounts of video data.
                
                A relational database is not appropriate for storing video binaries.

Why object storage?
                extremely durable
                highly scalable
                inexpensive compared with database storage
                designed for large objects
                integrates naturally with CDN


