15. Adaptive Bitrate Streaming

                This is an important YouTube concept.
                
                Instead of downloading one huge video file:
                
                                video.mp4
                
                we divide it into small segments.

                                For example:
                                
                                segment1
                                segment2
                                segment3
                                segment4
                                ...

The client can choose the appropriate bitrate for each segment.

Conceptually:
                
                Network Good
                
                1080p
                  ↓
                1080p
                  ↓
                1080p
                
                
                Network deteriorates
                
                1080p
                  ↓
                720p
                  ↓
                480p

This dramatically improves playback experience.
================================================================================================================================================================
16. HLS / DASH
                We can use adaptive streaming protocols such as:                
                        HLS
                        MPEG-DASH
                
                Conceptually:

                        Manifest
                        
                            ↓
                        
                        1080p playlist
                        720p playlist
                        480p playlist
                        360p playlist
                        
                            ↓
                        
                        Video segments

The client downloads the manifest and selects segments based on available bandwidth.

