36. The Most Important L5 Insight

        If the interviewer asks:        
                "What is the most important architectural decision here?"
        
        I'd answer:        
                “Separating video delivery from application logic.”
        
        Explain:

                Control Plane
                
                        API Gateway
                             ↓
                        Services
                             ↓
                        Metadata / Search / Auth
                
                
                Data Plane
                
                        CDN
                         ↓
                        Object Storage
                         ↓
                        Video Segments


Why?

        Because video traffic is orders of magnitude larger than metadata traffic.
        
        If you mix them:
                your application tier becomes the bottleneck.
                
        By separating them:

                API traffic → scalable services                
                Video traffic → CDN + object storage
        
        we can independently scale both workloads.
        
        That is the kind of architectural reasoning I'd want you to demonstrate at L5.
